# The completion check (decision 0081): a commit whose subject opens
# `feat(cut:<id>): ` is compared with the ledger, and when the ledger does not show
# cut <id> complete, a warning naming the cut, its phase and every work package not
# approved is written to this commit's output, asking its author to report the gap
# as a defect in how the ledger captures the harness's events. It is silent
# otherwise, never refuses (the commit is already made) and never writes the
# ledger. It is `cratylus completion-check`, run from source (`tsx`), as the
# immutability gate is, so it needs no build.
pnpm --silent --filter @cratylus/runtime completion-check || true
